of sync with His divine calendar. Humanity was slipping further and further away, the world falling into damnation, because of its discord with the perfect harmony of God. The faithful, like Franco, must take action in order to restore the proper timing sequence and return the world to grace. Thus Franco targets those he views are out of step with time: the young who act older than they are, the old who act too immature, survivors of previous accidents that should have killed them. In removing their hearts, the seat of the soul, and replacing them with clocks that strike to match the moment of death, he sends the proper signals to God that those responsible for the mistiming of the world have been restored to the proper cycle.<br /> <br /> Is the so-called Clockwork Killer insane? Clearly. But is he touched by the (clock)hand of God? Perhaps an angel of the God-Machine did indeed visit him\u2014that's what I think happened. He's completely mortal but also influenced by the God-Machine. You could use him in any kind of chronicle, including <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>. It could serve to unsettle even the undead, hinting at dark forces beyond Kindred conception. The implications are terrifying. Tell yourself he's just some psycho, but in the back of your mind you have to wonder....</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, it occurs to me that the Clockwork Killer would work really well in a <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b>game. Maybe true vampires are a bit outside of his scope, but you know who'd be the prime candidates for divine excision? Ghouls. People sustained beyond the flow of time by the blood of monsters. Their very existence defies God's perfect timing for the universe. When he starts killing ghouls, the Kindred take notice. How is he finding them? Is it the work of a rival? Is the killer fed their coordinates in his dreams by an angel, or does he have superior investigative skills that allow him to pierce the veil of the Masquerade? Will you keep all your ghouls with you at all times, and will that be enough? If a player character's ghoul is killed, that's a perfect way to draw them personally into the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus. How do I go about joining your game?<br /> <br /> Seriously, that's a pretty stellar idea for a story. Kudos.<br /> <br /> I'll probably eventually have the players flirt tangentially with the supernatural outside the Danse Macabre eventually. I don't want to go full crossover, but hinting at grand mysteries they can't unravel will just further underscore the tone of isolation and myopic intrigue that defines Requiem. That's a long way off though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-31-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:00:49-07:00","id":745343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/730307-the-god-machine-in-requiem?p=745332#post745332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus. How do I go about joining your game?<br /> <br /> Seriously, that's a pretty stellar idea for a story. Kudos.<br /> <br /> I'll probably eventually have the players flirt tangentially with the supernatural outside the Danse Macabre eventually. I don't want to go full crossover, but hinting at grand mysteries they can't unravel will just further underscore the tone of isolation and myopic intrigue that defines Requiem. That's a long way off though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you kindly! I'm flattered. If you want to steal the idea, by all means go ahead. I've got lots more. As far as my game, it's pretty full, but I might be able to add another player soon. Do you play PBP games? Do you play <b>Werewolf </b>or <b>Changeling</b>? I don't want to go full-on all-types-welcome sandbox yet, but maybe some day (and with a Co-ST)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T02:21:33-08:00","id":746230,"title":"","content":"I'd be very interested in playing in one of your games. I've seen you over on RPOL, but I thought it'd be creepy to just pop in and say hi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:05:33-08:00","id":746639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/730307-the-god-machine-in-requiem?p=745343#post745343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you kindly! I'm flattered. If you want to steal the idea, by all means go ahead. I've got lots more. As far as my game, it's pretty full, but I might be able to add another player soon. Do you play PBP games? Do you play <b>Werewolf </b>or <b>Changeling</b>? I don't want to go full-on all-types-welcome sandbox yet, but maybe some day (and with a Co-ST)!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was making a joke, but I actually might be interested. I haven't so much as glanced at Werewolf, but I like Changeling a great deal.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming PBP means play-by-post? Presumably message boards? I haven't, but I'm amenable to the idea. I have experience with chat-based play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:00:55-08:00","id":747269,"title":"","content":"I'm totally up for Werewolf, in general. I've only got to run it a little, and have really wanted to play. (Also, Claire, your zombie werewolf you posted gave me devious ideas. xD)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:51:09-08:00","id":761780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/730307-the-god-machine-in-requiem?p=745343#post745343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you kindly! I'm flattered. If you want to steal the idea, by all means go ahead. I've got lots more. As far as my game, it's pretty full, but I might be able to add another player soon. Do you play PBP games? Do you play <b>Werewolf </b>or <b>Changeling</b>? I don't want to go full-on all-types-welcome sandbox yet, but maybe some day (and with a Co-ST)!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was visiting this thread out of interest in the subject matter (I've written a Bloodline that may or may not be a piece of Elimination Infrastructure, and I have been using the Architects of the Monolith as it's servants for ages by now.)<br /> <br /> And then I saw your idea for the Clockwork Killer, which is a wonderful one. And I couldn't help but think how his activities must look like to a Mekhet. He commits mysterious killings and always leaves his calling card which must look pretty weird under Auspex. <br /> <br /> He might even be good Embrace material...<br /> <br /> And the I heard talk of a Werewolf game which sounds very interesting, I wonder if there is room for one player more?<br /> <br /> (I don't hope this came out too blunt and/or rude.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 11-10-2015, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg"